    "bio": "A Representative from New Jersey; born in Elizabeth, Union County, N.J., September 1, 1931; B.S., Rutgers University, New Brunswick, N.J., 1953; M.B.A., Seton Hall University Graduate School of Business Administration, South Orange, N.J., 1959; D.P.A., New York University, School of Public Administration, 1979; member, Union Township Zoning Board of Adjustment, 1962-1963; Union County Board of Freeholders, 1963-1964; State senate, 1967-1972; elected as a Republican to the Ninety-third and to the nine succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1973-January 3, 1993); was not a candidate for renomination in 1992 to the One Hundred Third Congress; died on October 13, 2008, in West Caldwell, N.J.; interment at Saint Teresa Cemetery, Summit, N.J.",
